      "message": "I agree, for this case, we want to have `p_disc_cb ` to trigger retry, \n\nbut my concern is, \n1. based on `HFP/HF/ACS/BV-05-C [HF initiated audio setup, AG has eSCO]`, HF can request eSCO connection. So only handling phone originated case may not be enough\n2. in original code, `btm_sco_connection_failed`, there are cases where it does not want `p_disc_cb` to have codec fallback and retry. Although I have not dive into the detail as it is very old code, but seems to be reasonable for some case, e.g. HCI_ERR_LMP_ERR_TRANS_COLLISION\n\nso I feel it maybe not that safe to change all of them. \n\nand in b/351301741#comment18, I request for verbose logging to discover more. But QA have not enabled yet in the new log. I will follow up on that",
